SpectraFuse: an independent implementation inspired by SpectRAG
=================================================================

SpectraFuse (Python package `spectrafuse`, published as `spectrag` until version 0.1.4) is an
independent implementation inspired by SpectRAG, the method described in:

  Zafer Sahinoglu, Abdulazeez Mohammed, Buse Yaren Kazangirler and Cahit Berkay Kazangirler.
  SpectRAG: Weighted Chunk Graphs for Token-Budgeted Context Selection in Multi-Hop
  Retrieval-Augmented Generation. arXiv:2610.36991, 2026. https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.36991

SpectraFuse is not SpectRAG and not an official release. It is not affiliated with or endorsed
by the paper's authors, and differences in its behaviour or results are its own.

SpectRAG's official implementation and releases are maintained by the authors at:

  https://github.com/SightAndCite/SpectRAG
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 The SpectRAG Authors

SpectraFuse was written from the paper. It does not include code from the official
implementation. The method, its equations, tables and default values are the work of the
paper's authors; please cite the paper if you use the method.

